# Always deploy to live

Joel is the only user. There is no separate staging/test environment to hand off to.

When a feature or fix is ready to use:

1. **Commit** the change (unless he explicitly says not to).
2. **Push to `main`** so Vercel production (`app.crowdsourcechoir.com`) picks it up.
3. **Confirm** the GitHub/Vercel deploy status succeeds before telling him it’s live.
4. Do **not** leave finished work only on a local branch, Preview-only branch, or “ask before push” by default.

Exceptions (ask first): secrets, destructive DB migrations, force-push, or anything he marked as WIP/experiment.
